        "requiredForDiagnosis": false
      }
    ],
    "minimumForDiagnosis": "Presence of ventricular septal defect with aortic valve cusp prolapse causing aortic regurgitation confirmed by echocardiography",
    "notes": "Diagnosis relies heavily on imaging and clinical correlation; early detection is critical to prevent progressive aortic valve damage."
